        <briefdescription>
<para>Maps a client group to its session table via a fixed allowlist. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Table names cannot be bound as query parameters, so interpolation is restricted to the two known groups; any other value is rejected instead of interpolated. <parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">group</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para><ref refid="controller_8hpp_1af928d8b9ced02f7387b9b56ed3877b11" kindref="member">Client</ref> group string. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>The table name, or std::nullopt for an unrecognized group.</para>
</simplesect>
SQL placeholders (like $1) can only stand for <emphasis>values</emphasis>, not for identifiers such as table names. So this function never pastes the caller&apos;s string directly into a query: it only accepts the two exact known groups and builds a safe table name. Anything else returns nullopt, and callers reject the request. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
